# SpeakEasy
A Guild Wars 2 Text-to-Speech Companion App

## Project Overview
Build a lightweight, external C#/.NET companion application for Guild Wars 2 that captures in-game text (NPC dialogue, messages, chat) via OCR and converts it to speech using TTS. The app must be non-invasive, ToS-compliant, performant, and easy to install/configure.

## Core Architecture Principles

### 1. External Companion App (NOT Injected Plugin)
- **CRITICAL**: This is a standalone desktop application, NOT a DLL injection or game client modification
- Never inject code into `Gw2-64.exe` or modify the game process
- Operate as a separate Windows process that reads screen content externally
- Position as an accessibility aid, not a game modification tool
- Use only screen capture, OCR, and audio playback - no game memory access or automation

### 2. Text Capture Strategy
- Use **OCR (Optical Character Recognition)** on a bounded screen region containing the chat panel
- Capture the chat box area periodically (5-15 FPS recommended)
- Maintain a rolling buffer of recent lines with deduplication
- Detect new lines by comparing against a hash-based seen set
- Handle game scaling, resolution changes, and window positioning

### 3. Text-to-Speech Implementation
- Support both **cloud TTS** (Google TTS, Play.ht, Azure Cognitive Services) and **local TTS** (Windows SAPI)
- Default to local TTS for zero-latency and offline capability
- Implement voice selection and configuration
- Queue TTS requests to prevent audio overlap/spam
- Apply rate limiting to avoid overwhelming TTS during fast-scrolling chat

### 4. Channel Filtering & Classification
- Filter text by channel type: NPC dialogue, story messages, party chat, guild chat, map chat, etc.
- Use color heuristics from GW2 chat panel conventions:
  - NPC text: darker sea green heading, grey/white text
  - Story text: specific color patterns
  - Chat channels: different colors per channel
- Allow user configuration of which channels to read aloud
- Provide presets: "NPC & Story Only", "Party/Squad/Guild", "All Chat"

## Technical Implementation Guidelines

### C# / .NET Framework
- Target **.NET 6+** or **.NET Framework 4.8** (depending on compatibility requirements)
- Use **WinForms** or **WPF** for the UI (prefer lightweight WinForms for minimal overhead)
- Implement as a **tray application** with minimal UI footprint
- Use async/await for all I/O operations (screen capture, OCR, TTS API calls)

### Screen Capture
- Use `System.Drawing` and Windows API calls for efficient screen region capture
- Consider libraries like `ScreenCapture.NET` or direct Win32 API via P/Invoke
- Capture only the chat panel region (configurable coordinates)
- Handle multi-monitor setups and windowed/fullscreen game modes
- Optimize capture frequency based on system performance

### OCR Integration
- Use **Tesseract OCR** via wrapper (e.g., `Tesseract.NET` or `IronOCR`)
- Pre-process images: contrast enhancement, color filtering, noise reduction
- Extract text line-by-line with timestamp tracking
- Implement smart deduplication: hash-based + time-based (ignore duplicates within 2-3 seconds)

### TTS Engine Integration
- **Local TTS (Primary)**:
  - Use `System.Speech.Synthesis.SpeechSynthesizer` for Windows SAPI
  - Support voice selection (Microsoft Zira, David, etc.)
  - Use `SpeakAsync()` for non-blocking playback
  - Implement audio queue management
  
- **Cloud TTS (Optional)**:
  - Support Google Cloud TTS, Azure Cognitive Services, or Play.ht
  - Implement API key management (secure storage)
  - Handle network failures gracefully (fallback to local TTS)
  - Cache frequently used phrases if possible

### Performance Optimization
- Keep memory footprint small (< 100MB ideally)
- Use efficient data structures (HashSet for deduplication, Queue for TTS)
- Minimize CPU usage: optimize OCR frequency, use threading appropriately
- Avoid blocking the UI thread: use BackgroundWorker or Task.Run
- Implement resource cleanup: dispose of image objects, close file handles

### Configuration & Settings
- Store settings in JSON or XML config file (user's AppData folder)
- Configurable options:
  - Chat region coordinates (with calibration tool)
  - Enabled channels (checkboxes per channel type)
  - TTS provider selection (Local/Cloud)
  - Voice selection and speech rate
  - Hotkeys (toggle on/off, pause, skip current)
  - Rate limiting (min time between TTS calls)
- Provide a simple settings window accessible from system tray

### Installation & Distribution
- Create a single executable or simple installer
- No complex dependencies: bundle OCR libraries if needed, or use NuGet packages
- Auto-detect GW2 installation path (optional, for future enhancements)
- First-run wizard for initial setup (calibrate chat region, test TTS)
- Provide clear documentation on ToS compliance

## Code Quality Standards

### Error Handling
- Gracefully handle OCR failures (bad image quality, no text detected)
- Handle TTS failures (API errors, network issues) with fallback
- Log errors to a file for debugging (optional, user-configurable)
- Never crash the app - catch all exceptions and show user-friendly messages

### Threading & Concurrency
- Screen capture: dedicated thread or timer
- OCR processing: background thread/Task
- TTS playback: async methods, queue-based
- UI updates: use Invoke/BeginInvoke for thread-safe updates
- Avoid race conditions with proper locking (lock, SemaphoreSlim, etc.)

### Resource Management
- Implement IDisposable pattern for all disposable resources
- Dispose of Bitmap objects immediately after OCR
- Close file streams properly
- Release audio resources when stopping TTS

### Code Organization
- Separate concerns: ScreenCapture, OCRProcessor, TTSManager, ConfigManager
- Use dependency injection where appropriate
- Keep classes focused and single-purpose
- Document public APIs with XML comments

## ToS Compliance & Safety

### What We DO
- ✅ Read screen content externally (like a screen reader)
- ✅ Play audio through system audio
- ✅ Respond to user hotkeys via global keyboard hooks
- ✅ Store configuration locally

### What We DON'T DO
- ❌ Inject DLLs into Gw2-64.exe
- ❌ Modify game memory or files
- ❌ Send automated inputs (keyboard/mouse)
- ❌ Intercept network traffic
- ❌ Automate gameplay in any way

### User Communication
- Include disclaimer in README about ToS compliance
- Recommend users verify with ArenaNet support if concerned
- Position as accessibility/immersion enhancement tool
- Provide clear instructions for safe usage

## Testing Considerations
- Test with different screen resolutions and scaling (100%, 125%, 150%)
- Test in windowed, windowed fullscreen, and fullscreen modes
- Test with fast-scrolling chat (rate limiting)
- Test TTS with long messages (queue management)
- Test error scenarios (network failures, OCR failures)
- Performance testing: CPU/memory usage during extended play

